{
  "opening": "This release introduces the new TLRU cache algorithm and enhances the existing time-to-live caches with improved expiration handling. It also adds several new key generation utilities and decorator features to improve caching flexibility and introspection.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The library must provide a new TLRUCache class that implements the Time-LRU cache algorithm, supporting standard mapping operations like get, set, pop, and clear. This class should behave similarly to other cache implementations in terms of interface but enforce eviction based on both recency and time-to-live constraints."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "Time-aware cache classes such as TTLCache and TLRUCache must correctly handle expiration logic where items are considered expired if their expiration time is less than or equal to the current timer value. The internal state management for these caches must ensure consistent behavior regarding currsize and maxsize limits during expiration events."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "Decorators such as @cached and @cachedmethod must expose their configuration parameters (e.g., maxsize, ttl) as attributes on the wrapper function object. These attributes should be readable after decoration to allow introspection of the cache settings applied to the wrapped function."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "The keys module must export a methodkey function that generates cache keys based on the method's self argument and its arguments, suitable for use with @cachedmethod. This complements existing hashkey and typedkey functions by providing a specialized key generator for instance methods."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "Cached decorators including @cached and @cachedmethod must include a cache_clear function or attribute that allows clearing all entries from the associated cache instance. Calling this function should reset the cache size to zero and invalidate any existing cached results."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "The @cached decorator must provide a cache_info function or attribute that returns statistics about the cache, such as hits, misses, and current size. This information should be accessible without modifying the decorated function's signature or behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m65",
      "text": "The keys module must export a typedmethodkey decorator that combines type checking with method key generation, ensuring that cached results are distinct based on argument types and method context. This decorator should be usable directly on methods or passed to caching decorators to enforce strict type-based caching."
    },
    {
      "id": "m69",
      "text": "The MRUCache class must be marked as deprecated, emitting a deprecation warning when instantiated or used. Users should be directed to use alternative cache implementations such as LRU or TTL variants instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "m71",
      "text": "The expire method on TTLCache must return an iterable of (key, value) pairs representing the items that were removed due to expiration. This allows callers to process or log expired entries before they are permanently discarded from the cache."
    },
    {
      "id": "m72",
      "text": "The expire method on TLRUCache must return an iterable of (key, value) pairs representing the items that were removed due to expiration. This ensures consistent behavior with TTLCache regarding the visibility of expired items during cleanup operations."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public APIs mentioned above are tested for correct behavior and that deprecation warnings are properly emitted where applicable. Documentation should be updated to reflect the new TLRUCache class and the enhanced key generation options."
}
